Bugfix: A new web upload is no longer restarted right away after a pause

The stall watchdog of the web upload compared against the time of the last
progress of the previous upload. When a new upload started more than a minute
after the previous one and reported 0 bytes at its first tick, the watchdog
took it for stalled and aborted and restarted it immediately. The time is now
reset whenever an upload starts.
